Description:
    Creates the folder structure, base files, and routes/constants insertion
    points for a new top-level module (e.g. Electrical) - the prerequisite
    step before scaffolding any model inside that module.

    Pass the module name in CamelCase. Nested sub-modules are not properly
    supported yet - avoid them.

    Creates app/models/<module>/base.rb (the shared parent class for every
    model in the module), locale folders for every configured language, a
    constants file, and inserts routing/constants markers used by the
    scaffold generator afterward.

    After running, open app/models/<module>/base.rb and set its default
    swatch and discipline name if they shouldn't just match the module name.

Examples:
    `bin/rails generate project_assistant:module Electrical`
